  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Public Investment Management Through Sustainable Public Procurement Capacity Building in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the grant is to help meet Caribbean citizens&apos; demands for the timely, cost-effective and efficient delivery of high-quality public services, across a broad range of sectors, by improving the performance of Caribbean countries&apos; public investment programs through the creation of a sustainable, local institution which will produce qualified, professional procurement officers for the public service. The development objective of the grant is to establish a sustainable professional procurement training and accreditation institution in the Caribbean region. This institution will provide professional and technical training programs in procurement, leading to theaward of internationally-recognized professional qualifications in procurement, thereby producing, within the region, a cadre of qualified, well-trained procurement professionals for public service throughout the Caribbean and providing Caribbean governments witha regional resource center that will allow them to build their procurement capacity and maintain it over the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
